UID:10005697-1787922000-1787929200@sdlancaster.org
SUMMARY:Valued Volunteers – Together We Read
DESCRIPTION:The School District of Lancaster is inviting community members to become part of Valued Volunteers – Together We Read\, a districtwide initiative that connects volunteers with students to help strengthen reading skills on Monday\, July 27\, at 1:00 pm – 3:00 pm at the Scheffey Professional Learning Center located at 1020 Lehigh Ave. Lancaster PA.   \nTHIS EVENT has been rescheduled from Monday\, July 27.  \nThe training serves as both the district’s required Valued Volunteers orientation and a kickoff for the Together We Read initiative. Participants will learn about the volunteer process while also receiving reading strategies\, tips\, and resources they can use when reading with students in our schools. \nNo teaching experience is necessary. If you’re a first-time volunteer or returning to support SDoL students\, the training will provide the tools and confidence needed to make every reading session meaningful. \n \nVolunteers play an important role in helping students build literacy skills and a love of reading. By sharing your time\, you can make a lasting difference in a child’s educational journey. \nJoin us for an upcoming Valued Volunteers – Together We Read training and discover how you can help students grow\, one story at a time.
URL:https://sdlancaster.org/event/valued-volunteers-together-we-read/
LOCATION:Scheffey Professional Learning Center\, 1020 Lehigh Avenue\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Burrowes Elementary,Districtwide Events
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR